1
00:00:06,005 --> 00:00:09,259
-[insects chirping]
-[rumbling]

2
00:00:12,011 --> 00:00:14,764
[dinosaurs bellowing]

3
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:40,248
[thudding]

4
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:46,463
[roars, screeches]

5
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:50,925
[alarm blaring]

6
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:58,183
[all panting]

7
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:04,647
[male voice] Attention. All park-goers
must report to the South Ferry Dock

8
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:06,399
for immediate evacuation.

9
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:09,819
-Last ferry departs in two hours.
-[panting continues]

10
00:01:09,903 --> 00:01:13,531
That's it? No explanations?
That's all we get?

11
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:14,741
[Darius panting]

12
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:19,329
We have to move. The only way
we're gonna make it is if we run.

13
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:21,790
-Um...
-[Yasmina grunting]

14
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:24,375
Are we sure that's the best way
to get there?

15
00:01:24,459 --> 00:01:25,668
I'm fine.

16
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:27,504
I've competed with a torn ACL.

17
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:29,881
You should be way more worried
about Ben and Bumpy.

18
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:31,633
[Ben panting]

19
00:01:31,716 --> 00:01:34,969
What we should all be worried about
is catching a boat out of here

20
00:01:35,053 --> 00:01:37,514
and, naturally, we have a problem.

21
00:01:38,014 --> 00:01:39,265
We're here.

22
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:41,851
The docks are on the southern tip
of the island.

23
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:43,937
Even if we ran at peak Yaz speed,

24
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:45,897
there's no way we'd make
the last boat out.

25
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,315
You don't know that.

26
00:01:47,398 --> 00:01:48,316
[scoffs] Yes, I do.

27
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:51,611
I memorized the evacuation plan
on the ferry ride over.

28
00:01:51,694 --> 00:01:53,738
[all groan]

29
00:01:53,822 --> 00:01:55,824
Okay, so we need another way.

30
00:01:56,282 --> 00:01:57,283
Um...

31
00:01:58,868 --> 00:01:59,744
Can we use those somehow?

32
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:02,038
Or send someone to tell the ferry people
to wait?

33
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:04,332
-Or...
-Or make a few jetpacks real quick?

34
00:02:04,415 --> 00:02:08,002
Oh! We should befriend a unicorn!

35
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:10,713
Face it. It's hopeless.

36
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:13,758
[automated voice] We will be arriving
at Main Street--

37
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:15,885
-your destination for fine dining...
-Is that...?

38
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:18,138
...and shopping at Jurassic World.

39
00:02:18,763 --> 00:02:21,808
Followed by stops
at the Jurassic World Lagoon

40
00:02:21,891 --> 00:02:23,768
and the South Ferry Dock.

41
00:02:24,561 --> 00:02:26,396
Monorail, what-what!

42
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:30,066
-Mm, nicely played, Universe.
-Hurry!

43
00:02:33,611 --> 00:02:35,989
[all panting]

44
00:02:36,072 --> 00:02:37,407
[Darius] We gotta move!

45
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:38,950
[both panting]

46
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:42,871
It's nice havin' some company back here
for once.

47
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:44,205
I'm fine.

48
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:45,957
[sighs]

49
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:48,960
[panting]

50
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:52,130
-[Kenji exclaims]
-[laughing]

51
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:53,506
[Brooklynn] Oh, no.

52
00:02:58,928 --> 00:03:00,638
Shh!

53
00:03:06,144 --> 00:03:08,855
-[growling]
-[gasps, pants]

54
00:03:22,827 --> 00:03:23,745
[whispers] Move.

55
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:35,715
[growling continues]

56
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:46,267
-[snarls]
-[all gasp]

57
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:54,651
[gasps]

58
00:03:55,276 --> 00:03:56,110
[grunts]

59
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:00,698
-[grunts]
-[clatters]

60
00:04:00,782 --> 00:04:03,534
[snarls, growls]

61
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:28,977
[growls]

62
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:35,650
[gasps]

63
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:40,321
[Yasmina pants]

64
00:04:57,505 --> 00:04:58,339
[gasps]

65
00:04:59,841 --> 00:05:02,051
[gasping]

66
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:05,471
[sighs]

67
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:15,189
Mon--!

68
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:18,192
Shh!

69
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:24,324
[automated voice] Welcome to
the Jurassic World Lagoon.

70
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:28,202
-Next stop, Ferry Landing!
-[roars]

71
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:29,746
-[Darius] Run!
-[Ben whimpers]

72
00:05:32,915 --> 00:05:34,751
-[roars]
-[yelps, pants]

73
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:43,801
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

74
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:46,095
[Ben screaming]

75
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:50,349
-[gasps]
-[Yasmina grunts]

76
00:05:55,229 --> 00:05:58,775
-[grunts, pants]
-[roars]

77
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:02,028
[automated voice] Please stand clear
of the closing doors.

78
00:06:02,111 --> 00:06:02,945
[Kenji grunts]

79
00:06:03,863 --> 00:06:05,656
[Ben and Yasmina grunting]

80
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,452
-[whimpers]
-[grunting]

81
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:11,829
-[snarling]
-[Darius] Ben! Out of the way!

82
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,876
-[Yasmina whimpers]
-[roars]

83
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:19,629
[Ben and Yasmina scream]

84
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:23,216
-[whimpers]
-[roars]

85
00:06:28,721 --> 00:06:31,641
-Please stand-- Please stand--
-Do not let those doors close!

86
00:06:32,391 --> 00:06:33,851
[roaring]

87
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:37,355
-[Yasmina grunting]
-[roars]

88
00:06:40,858 --> 00:06:41,943
[thuds]

89
00:06:42,568 --> 00:06:43,945
-[grunts]
-[Ben yelps]

90
00:06:44,028 --> 00:06:45,446
-[Kenji grunts]
-[Yasmina pants]

91
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:46,614
Doors closing.

92
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:50,868
[roaring]

93
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:55,998
No way.

94
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:58,543
Something bad always happens
when we think we're safe.

95
00:06:58,626 --> 00:07:00,711
Watch. The doors are gonna open.

96
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:03,131
-[scoffs]
-Oh, okay,

97
00:07:03,214 --> 00:07:07,260
then, the train's gonna stop
because that's how this works.

98
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:10,054
I'm pretty sure we're safe now.

99
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:12,807
Well, we were until you said that.

100
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:26,195
[Dave] I'll check here,
you check the stadium.

101
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:28,906
[Roxie] Kids?

102
00:07:29,073 --> 00:07:31,617
-Darius?
-[Dave] Brooklynn?

103
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:33,035
[Roxie] Anybody here?

104
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:37,165
[panting]

105
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:46,757
Oh, no.

106
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:48,134
They made it out!

107
00:07:48,593 --> 00:07:51,679
These look both posh and tacky enough
to be something Kenji would wear.

108
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:53,055
[Dave sighs]

109
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:55,266
They're okay. I know it.

110
00:07:55,349 --> 00:07:58,144
[automated voice] Welcome to
the Jurassic World Lagoon.

111
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:04,400
The kids? They're alive!

112
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:05,651
Hey, guys!

113
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:09,238
-[Roxie] Hey!
-Kids! Kids! Dang it.

114
00:08:09,322 --> 00:08:11,324
[male voice] Attention.
All park-goers must report

115
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:14,160
to the South Ferry Dock
for immediate evacuation.

116
00:08:14,243 --> 00:08:16,204
Last ferry departs in 90 minutes.

117
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:19,874
-They're headed to the docks!
-Then it's time to ship out!

118
00:08:19,957 --> 00:08:21,542
[roaring]

119
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:25,922
Or let's just go.

120
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,841
[roars]

121
00:08:28,925 --> 00:08:30,927
[crickets chirping]

122
00:08:36,432 --> 00:08:38,726
[Darius panting]

123
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:45,775
[sighs] It's over.

124
00:08:47,109 --> 00:08:50,196
Guys, we did it.

125
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:51,822
We're going home.

126
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:02,416
Whoo-hoo!

127
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,001
-[gasps]
-[Bumpy squeals]

128
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:08,798
Yeah! Whoo!

129
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:10,091
-[Darius laughs]
-Whoo!

130
00:09:10,174 --> 00:09:11,259
-Yeah!
-Yes!

131
00:09:11,342 --> 00:09:12,635
Yeah!

132
00:09:12,718 --> 00:09:13,761
[all laughing]

133
00:09:14,428 --> 00:09:16,389
-Finally!
-Alrighty!

134
00:09:17,181 --> 00:09:19,767
It's cool, man. We're good.

135
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:21,560
We'll be at the main dock soon.

136
00:09:21,852 --> 00:09:24,397
This calls for a celebration.

137
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,065
I might be able to help with that.

138
00:09:28,067 --> 00:09:30,278
Stashed a few treats for the road.

139
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:32,989
-Ooh, sweet!
-I'm starving!

140
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:34,699
Our little Ben is useful.

141
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:41,831
[all retching, spitting]

142
00:09:41,914 --> 00:09:42,999
[Sammy] This is nasty.

143
00:09:43,082 --> 00:09:45,001
Get it off! Get it off!

144
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:49,422
Ben, someone stole your candy bars
and put dirt in 'em.

145
00:09:49,505 --> 00:09:52,258
They're carob bars.
They pair perfectly with--

146
00:09:52,341 --> 00:09:53,676
Carob juice.

147
00:09:53,926 --> 00:09:54,844
Awesome.

148
00:09:55,094 --> 00:09:57,138
Carob is nature's chocolate.

149
00:09:57,221 --> 00:10:00,474
Just as delicious, with none of the sugar
or caffeine.

150
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:03,936
What's wrong with sugar and caffeine?

151
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:08,274
First thing I'm gonna do when I get home
is hug my espresso machine.

152
00:10:08,774 --> 00:10:10,276
I may never let go.

153
00:10:10,359 --> 00:10:14,905
You know... [clears throat] I've often
described myself as a tall, hot drink.

154
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:15,823
[all scoffing]

155
00:10:16,157 --> 00:10:17,450
-Come on, man.
-Gross.

156
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:20,036
You could never be coffee.

157
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:22,538
[scoffs] I could be coffee.

158
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:24,332
I cannot wait to be home.

159
00:10:24,415 --> 00:10:27,251
Once my ankle's better,
it's back to training.

160
00:10:27,335 --> 00:10:29,462
And I guess finding
a new corporate sponsor,

161
00:10:29,545 --> 00:10:32,089
since mine was Jurassic World.

162
00:10:32,173 --> 00:10:33,174
But you know...

163
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:35,843
It's gonna be weird for things
to be normal again.

164
00:10:35,926 --> 00:10:39,388
Like, are video games
gonna seem boring now? [chuckles]

165
00:10:39,555 --> 00:10:42,141
How about you? What's the first thing
you'll do when you get home?

166
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:44,602
Depends on which wing of our mansion
you're talkin' about.

167
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:48,272
East wing is usually off limits,
but Dad and Candy are away on business,

168
00:10:48,356 --> 00:10:52,735
so I guess I'll go downstairs
to our bowling alley. [chuckles]

169
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:56,447
Staff always lets me win.

170
00:10:57,656 --> 00:10:59,367
Life of a VIP.

171
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:02,411
So, what have you missed, Ben?

172
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:03,913
[Kenji] Oh. Let me guess,

173
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:08,334
you can't wait to get home to your closet
of dork pouches.

174
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:11,504
-[Brooklynn and Sammy chuckle]
-Ha, ha. Very funny.

175
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:14,423
Seriously, Ben, you've had juice boxes
for days!

176
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:16,384
How much stuff can you fit in that thing?

177
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:18,761
One, lots, and two,

178
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:22,556
obviously the first thing I'm gonna do
when I get back is restock it.

179
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:24,934
[all laughing]

180
00:11:27,311 --> 00:11:29,230
Check it out.
[imitates lightsaber powering up]

181
00:11:30,439 --> 00:11:31,273
[Ben and Brooklynn grunt]

182
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:35,861
I found the first thing at Jurassic World
that works!

183
00:11:39,698 --> 00:11:40,991
[chuckles] Still works.

184
00:11:41,283 --> 00:11:44,412
I still can't believe how much went wrong.
[chuckles]

185
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:46,330
Like that time we almost got eaten?

186
00:11:46,414 --> 00:11:47,665
Which time?

187
00:11:47,748 --> 00:11:50,626
How was there more than one time?

188
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:55,923
Let's all raise our carob juice.

189
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:57,425
A toast!

190
00:11:57,925 --> 00:11:59,301
To not getting eaten!

191
00:11:59,593 --> 00:12:02,430
-To not getting eaten!
-To not getting eaten!

192
00:12:02,513 --> 00:12:04,306
[slurping]

193
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:07,309
[grunts] Ugh!

194
00:12:08,602 --> 00:12:09,854
[Yasmina groans]

195
00:12:11,355 --> 00:12:14,150
-[spits]
-[slurps, sighs]

196
00:12:14,483 --> 00:12:16,235
[Brooklynn shudders]

197
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:20,823
-To no more running away!
-To no more running away!

198
00:12:21,532 --> 00:12:24,076
-[slurps]
-[Darius chuckles]

199
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:25,786
[Brooklynn] Hmm.

200
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:28,122
Mm-mm.

201
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:31,834
[slurps, sighs]

202
00:12:31,917 --> 00:12:34,462
To the return of a low-level gnawing dread

203
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:37,965
rather than an all-encompassing
impending doom!

204
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:39,592
Why not!

205
00:12:39,675 --> 00:12:42,303
-[Brooklynn] To what Ben said!
-[Kenji] Bad doom versus normal doom!

206
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:44,346
-I got one. [gasps]
-[explosion]

207
00:12:44,513 --> 00:12:45,723
[all grunt]

208
00:12:45,806 --> 00:12:47,224
What was that?

209
00:12:47,516 --> 00:12:48,976
It sounded like an explosion.

210
00:12:49,059 --> 00:12:51,604
-Ugh! Not again!
-I don't see anything.

211
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:54,523
I don't think it was near us.

212
00:12:54,773 --> 00:12:56,775
We're okay. We're still okay.

213
00:13:02,698 --> 00:13:06,327
[Bumpy groans]

214
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:11,749
I know camp wasn't what we thought
it was gonna be.

215
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:13,751
But after everything we went through,

216
00:13:13,834 --> 00:13:16,754
at least we're leavin' this place
with five new friends!

217
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:20,299
To the six of us being best friends
for life!

218
00:13:20,382 --> 00:13:21,509
Clink!

219
00:13:26,555 --> 00:13:28,098
"No added sugars," wow.

220
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:29,850
[Sammy] Guys?

221
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:31,435
Hello?

222
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:34,688
Wait, do you guys not see us as friends?

223
00:13:35,564 --> 00:13:37,733
I mean... [sighs]

224
00:13:37,816 --> 00:13:40,319
Doesn't it usually take
more than a few days

225
00:13:40,402 --> 00:13:42,363
to become friends with someone?

226
00:13:42,571 --> 00:13:44,198
We were thrown together at random.

227
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:46,200
We have nothing in common.

228
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:49,036
That's not true!

229
00:13:49,119 --> 00:13:52,665
We've been through more together
than most friends have in a lifetime.

230
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:57,586
And now that it's over, what are the odds
that we'll ever see each other again?

231
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:05,302
[automated voice] Coming up on the right,
you'll see our world-renowned

232
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:08,389
18-hole, dinosaur-themed
golf course.

233
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:12,685
It's one of the many wonders
that makes this park so very Jurassic.

234
00:14:12,768 --> 00:14:15,104
[chuckles] What does that even mean?

235
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:17,231
I thought I knew.

236
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:22,653
My whole life, I had this idea
of Jurassic World.

237
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:28,450
My dad used to say this place was,
"All-osaurus and a bag of chips."

238
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,580
He was so corny.

239
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:35,291
Um, was?

240
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,459
So, your dad is...

241
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:49,597
I'm sorry, Darius.

242
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:53,475
Ugh! "Sorry." Nice one,
Sammy, ya ding-dong!

243
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:56,186
-Like "sorry" could begin to--
-It's okay.

244
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:00,983
Hey, at least your dad never saw

245
00:15:01,066 --> 00:15:04,111
what a dumpster fire this place turned out
to be, huh?

246
00:15:04,194 --> 00:15:05,779
Ow! What?

247
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:09,533
I meant it's cool that Darius and his dad
were so close.

248
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:10,868
I could count on one hand

249
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:14,246
the number of times me and my dad
have done... anything.

250
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:16,707
Kenji, that's just real sad.

251
00:15:17,207 --> 00:15:18,208
Yeah.

252
00:15:19,627 --> 00:15:21,754
Did I mention I have a bowling alley?

253
00:15:22,838 --> 00:15:23,839
[Ben] Dang it!

254
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:26,675
Come on, it's gotta be here somewhere.
Oh! [scoffs]

255
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:30,095
Bumpy stepped in something icky
and I'm low on sanitizer.

256
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,847
It's fine. I can make more.

257
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:33,682
Ben, why are you here?

258
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:38,604
What he means is--
Eh, well, you're scared of dinosaurs,

259
00:15:38,687 --> 00:15:42,232
and the outdoors,
and sometimes the indoors, and germs.

260
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:44,026
Whipped cream for some reason?

261
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:47,029
The way it moves. [shudders]

262
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:50,074
Yeah, that's what I'm talking about.
What's the deal?

263
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:51,283
[Bumpy squeals]

264
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:54,370
My mom works for Mr. Masrani.
She got me into camp.

265
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:58,999
Said it would be a great way for me
to "face my fears." It's been a nightmare!

266
00:15:59,083 --> 00:16:01,585
I'm sick of being scared all the time.

267
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:04,546
And of running,
and of almost getting eaten,

268
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:08,092
and... and of holding everyone back.

269
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:11,971
I just can't do... this.

270
00:16:17,559 --> 00:16:19,728
[Bumpy groans]

271
00:16:19,812 --> 00:16:22,147
[Ben] But it's not all bad.

272
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:24,733
If I hadn't come,
I-- I never would have met--

273
00:16:24,817 --> 00:16:26,402
-[crashing]
-[all gasp]

274
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:29,446
-[crashing]
-[all grunt]

275
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:32,741
[Darius panting]

276
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:36,412
-[crashing]
-[all yell]

277
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:44,670
Guys, we gotta turn off the lights!

278
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,673
-[smashing]
-[Darius grunting]

279
00:16:58,767 --> 00:17:01,895
-[gasps]
-[screeches]

280
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,483
Flying reptiles are basically seabirds.

281
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:08,318
They're attracted to shiny,
moving objects,

282
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:11,780
-and with all these lights on--
-We're a shiny, moving object!

283
00:17:11,864 --> 00:17:12,906
[screeches]

284
00:17:13,198 --> 00:17:14,074
[screams]

285
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:16,952
[Kenji panting]

286
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:18,704
What should I do?

287
00:17:18,787 --> 00:17:21,290
-Just keep out of the way!
-[smashing continues]

288
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:34,887
-[screeching]
-[whimpering]

289
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:37,222
[Yasmina and Sammy yelp]

290
00:17:37,514 --> 00:17:38,348
[grunting]

291
00:17:38,557 --> 00:17:40,851
-[whimpering]
-[grunting continues]

292
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,686
[electricity buzzes]

293
00:17:43,103 --> 00:17:45,355
[squawking]

294
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:48,859
[screeching]

295
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:51,737
-[whimpers, screams]
-[screeches]

296
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:58,285
[grunts] Brooklynn, you're with Yaz.

297
00:17:58,368 --> 00:18:00,079
Sammy, help Ben and Bumpy across!

298
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:03,624
[Yasmina pants] Whoa!

299
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:06,794
[grunts, thuds]

300
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,254
[Bumpy grunts]

301
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:12,257
[screeching]

302
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:23,143
[automated voice] Smile!
You're at Jurassic World.

303
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:26,814
We hope you're having...
[distorted voice] a Jurassic time.

304
00:18:29,066 --> 00:18:30,859
[yelps, grunts]

305
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:32,110
[Bumpy squeals]

306
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:35,364
-[crashing]
-[grunting, groaning]

307
00:18:35,906 --> 00:18:37,157
[gasps]

308
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:50,504
At least now we know
what that boom was earlier.

309
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:52,339
-I told you--
-[Brooklynn] Don't.

310
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:54,842
If we don't switch tracks
or stop this car right now,

311
00:18:54,925 --> 00:18:57,094
we're gonna hit that thing, full speed!

312
00:18:57,261 --> 00:18:59,263
The front car,
there's control panels there!

313
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:01,265
VIP Tour, I was eight, they let me drive.

314
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:04,726
[grunts] No, no, no!

315
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:07,813
-[Ben whimpering]
-[Bumpy groans]

316
00:19:07,896 --> 00:19:09,106
[all grunting]

317
00:19:11,149 --> 00:19:13,318
-[grunts, sighs]
-[screeching]

318
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:18,240
I'm gonna get to the control car
through there.

319
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:20,701
-You're gonna what?
-You can't go out there!

320
00:19:20,784 --> 00:19:22,703
[sputters] That's where
the flying whatevers are!

321
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,746
We don't have a choice! Me and--

322
00:19:29,668 --> 00:19:31,712
-I'm the only one who can fit.
-[screeches]

323
00:19:32,045 --> 00:19:33,213
-[yelps]
-[all yelp]

324
00:19:34,089 --> 00:19:35,966
[Bumpy groans]

325
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:42,639
You're gonna be okay.

326
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:46,185
Distract the flock while I crawl over
the top to the control car.

327
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:47,853
Use the flashlights, keep them away from--

328
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:49,438
-[hatch squeaks]
-[all gasp]

329
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:51,106
[Bumpy squeals]

330
00:19:51,607 --> 00:19:52,566
[gasps] Ben!

331
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:56,778
Ben, what are you doing?

332
00:20:00,073 --> 00:20:00,908
[grunts]

333
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:05,329
I can do this! Just distract them!

334
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:08,248
-[pants, screams]
-[screeches]

335
00:20:09,499 --> 00:20:11,084
Come on! We have to keep them away
from Ben!

336
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:13,253
[pants]

337
00:20:15,672 --> 00:20:19,134
[all panting]

338
00:20:19,801 --> 00:20:21,762
[screeches]

339
00:20:34,066 --> 00:20:35,067
I can do this.

340
00:20:36,276 --> 00:20:37,235
I can do this.

341
00:20:37,402 --> 00:20:38,278
[grunts]

342
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:41,823
-[all panting]
-[screeching]

343
00:20:43,575 --> 00:20:44,576
[whimpers]

344
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:47,579
[grunts]

345
00:20:48,497 --> 00:20:49,498
[yells]

346
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:52,042
[grunting]

347
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:55,879
[console trilling]

348
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,882
[whimpering]

349
00:21:00,926 --> 00:21:02,052
-[bangs]
-[screeches]

350
00:21:09,685 --> 00:21:12,813
[panting]

351
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:15,190
-[screeches]
-[screams]

352
00:21:20,153 --> 00:21:22,322
[crashing]

353
00:21:22,531 --> 00:21:23,532
[grunting]

354
00:21:28,036 --> 00:21:29,913
[crashes]

355
00:21:36,586 --> 00:21:38,630
[screeching]

356
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:43,051
[laughing, whooping]

357
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:47,723
-[pants, sighs]
-[Brooklynn] Yeah!

358
00:21:47,848 --> 00:21:52,185
[all chanting] Ben, Ben,
Ben, Ben, Ben, Ben!

359
00:21:52,269 --> 00:21:54,146
-[Ben laughs]
-[Bumpy groans]

360
00:21:55,355 --> 00:21:58,066
You saved us, Ben.
I didn't know you had it in you.

361
00:21:59,735 --> 00:22:02,696
[glass shatters]

362
00:22:06,783 --> 00:22:09,661
-Ben!
-[Ben screaming]

363
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:13,373
[grunting]

364
00:22:15,709 --> 00:22:18,170
-[Ben gasps, whimpers]
-[grunting]

365
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:24,801
-Oh, no!
-[grunting, screaming]

366
00:22:27,554 --> 00:22:28,722
[Ben] Help!

367
00:22:29,264 --> 00:22:32,476
-Hang on!
-[grunts] Darius! Darius! Darius!

368
00:22:32,559 --> 00:22:34,144
No! [grunts]

369
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:37,147
No! [screams]

370
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:45,781
[theme music playing]

